I have completed initial work on a wrapper for procmail to run it in a
new security context.  I've tested it along with spamassassin in some
simple configurations. I've attached both se_procmail.c and a README
file.

A number of modifications to the policy were needed.  If you're tracking
my arch tree, the required modifications are in patch-63 and patch-64. 
I've attached the diff associated with those patches, for convenience.

Now, I'm not quite sure where to put se_procmail.  It doesn't seem quite
right to put it in policycoreutils.  But it also feels like overkill to
put it in a separate package.  Ideas?
 

